{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (Task ID: 5459) to implement srd069-join R2.1-R2.4 in the go-unix-utils project. This involves:\n   - Implementing the core join logic in cmd/join/main.go by filling in the stub `joinFiles` function\n   - R2.1: -1 FIELD / -2 FIELD flags to select which field to join on for each file\n   - R2.2: -j FIELD to set join field for both files simultaneously\n   - R2.3: -o FORMAT for selecting and ordering output fields (FILENUM.FIELDNUM specifiers or '0' for join field)\n   - R2.4: -t CHAR for custom input/output field separator\n   - Creating cmd/join/join_test.go with differential tests against `gjoin` reference binary\n   - Acceptance criteria: go build, go test, go vet all pass; differential tests cover R2.1-R2.4 behaviors\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Relational join of two sorted files on a common field\n   - Differential testing pattern using pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests against GNU reference binary (gjoin)\n   - Field splitting by whitespace (default) or custom separator (-t)\n   - Output format specification with FILENUM.FIELDNUM notation\n   - SIGPIPE handler (sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler)\n   - LC_ALL=C for deterministic collation in tests\n   - Graceful skip when reference binary not found (exec.LookPath + t.Skip)\n   - The execution constitution mandates: no git commands, write all code before building, functions ≤40 lines, files ≤500 lines, SPDX copyright header\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd069-join.yaml** (read)\n     - Full SRD with R1 (default join), R2 (field selection/output format), R3 (unpairable/header), R4 (exit codes/testing)\n     - This task focuses on R2.1-R2.4 only\n     - Non-goals: no locale-a