{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VCzqkqrnRN6g5W5dKiA5Mx","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've found excellent examples of how file-based tests are structured using RunDiffTests. Here's what I found:\n\n## Summary\n\nI found two great examples in the cmd/ package showing how to create and use file-based test inputs with RunDiffTests:\n\n### Example 1: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5459/cmd/paste/paste_test.go`\n\nThis is a clean, concise example (119 lines total). The pattern:\n\n1. **Create temp directory**: `dir := t.TempDir()` (line 24)\n2. **Write test files**: Helper function `writeFile(t, dir, \"filename\", \"content\")` creates files in the temp dir (lines 25-28)\n3. **Reference files by name in Args**: Pass just the filename (relative to WorkDir) in the DiffTest Args field (e.g., `Args: []string{\"a.txt\", \"nums.txt\"}`)\n4. **Set WorkDir**: Point each test to the temp directory where files were created (e.g., `WorkDir: dir`)\n5. **Run tests**: `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)` (line 110)\n\nThe writeFile helper (lines 113-118) handles the file creation using `os.WriteFile()`.\n\n### Example 2: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5459/cmd/comm/comm_test.go`\n\nA more comprehensive example (404 lines) showing the same pattern at scale with many test files (lines 45-67) and 60+ test cases using those files with various flags and options (lines 71-362). The writeFile helper pattern is identical (lines 398-403).\n\nBoth examples show the key insight: **Files are created once in TempDir, then test cases reference them by relative filename while specifying WorkDir**, allowing RunDiffTests to properly resolve and execute them."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44cf73d0-a11e-4b9c-a1cb-e8a9f7a07078","uuid":"e0d57b86-66fe-4eb8-8a2c-c8e28da52872","timestamp":"2026-05-22T14:41:55.185Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5459, find a cmd/ package that has a test file using RunDiffTests with file-based test inputs (creating temp files in t.TempDir). I need to see how they create test files and pass file paths as args in DiffTest. Show me the test file content of one good example. Search breadth: quick.","agentId":"a5df6e402259d23a6","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've found excellent examples of how file-based tests are structured using RunDiffTests. Here's what I found:\n\n## Summary\n\nI found two great examples in the cmd/ package showing how to create and use file-based test inputs with RunDiffTests:\n\n### Example 1: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5459/cmd/paste/paste_test.go`\n\nThis is a clean, concise example (119 lines total). The pattern:\n\n1. **Create temp directory**: `dir := t.TempDir()` (line 24)\n2. **Write test files**: Helper function `writeFile(t, dir, \"filename\", \"content\")` creates files in the temp dir (lines 25-28)\n3. **Reference files by name in Args**: Pass just the filename (relative to WorkDir) in the DiffTest Args field (e.g., `Args: []string{\"a.txt\", \"nums.txt\"}`)\n4. **Set WorkDir**: Point each test to the temp directory where files were created (e.g., `WorkDir: dir`)\n5. **Run tests**: `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)` (line 110)\n\nThe writeFile helper (lines 113-118) handles the file creation using `os.WriteFile()`.\n\n### Example 2: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5459/cmd/comm/comm_test.go`\n\nA more comprehensive example (404 lines) showing the same pattern at scale with many test files (lines 45-67) and 60+ test cases using those files with various flags and options (lines 71-362). The writeFile helper pattern is identical (lines 398-403).\n\nBoth examples show the key insight: **Files are created once in TempDir, then test cases reference them by relative filename while specifying WorkDir**, allowing RunDiffTests to properly resolve and execute them."}],"totalDurationMs":16524,"totalTokens":27729,"totalToolUseCount":5,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5086,"cache_read_input_tokens":22134,"output_tokens":505,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5086},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":505,"cache_read_input_tokens":22134,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5086,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5086,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":2,"searchCount":2,"bashCount":1,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
